  message: "CLOSED done — PR #144, merged to dev as 38933e8f93 (2026-08-01).\n\nFIX: budget-monotone seed policy + budget-independent positional coverage\nstop, default path only (connectivity mode keeps its adaptive policy by\ndesign — bridging is not a ranked prefix and containment was never its\ncontract). Three mechanisms closed: the entrypoint cap's regime switch on\nlen(eps) > max_symbols, the shrinking cross-cutting budget\n(max//2 - len(forced)), and the coverage stop counting seed centrality.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (the item's own filed repro, re-run on the merged\ncode): the same 8-map sweep that measured 6/8 VIOLATED now reads 8/8 OK —\ncaddy/apollo/SwiftyJSON/zoxide/spring-petclinic/sherpa-csharp all\ncontainment-monotonic at --max-symbols 10/25/50/100 against the 07-17\nbakeoff maps; express and pretix stay clean. TestSeededContainment pins\nthe property in-suite across budgets straddling the regime boundary at\ntwo coverage targets, with feature-preservation guards (seeds included at\ngenerous budgets; seeds never consume the whole budget). 226 compact + 207\nCLI tests green.\n\nMethod note for the record: the first draft of the new test passed\nVACUOUSLY because its centrality-ladder edges used 'calls' — itself a\ncross-cutting type — so every node became a seed candidate and the seed\nmachinery was never isolated. The committed fixture uses 'references' and\ndocuments why. (L17's vacuous-green, caught before commit.)"  # ec89
